{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI hope the children are well and that Karl is not too absorbed in his studies tonight. I write from Paris, where the air is thick with September damp.\n\nYesterday I took a carriage to Saint-Cloud. The Seine was grey and sluggish, but the view from the terrace was grand enough to remind me that nature, however beautiful, lacks the inner movement of Spirit.\n\nTonight, however, I sat through a three-act ballet on a sleepwalker. It was absurd. The hero is found in a nobleman’s bed, then mimes crossing a roof with a lantern. Only the first act was actually danced; the rest was mere pantomime. The audience laughed, but I felt only a profound irritation. To see human freedom reduced to such mechanical, dream-like posturing is painful. It is a spirit asleep, yet it does not even have the dignity of true slumber.\n\nI miss our walks in the Tiergarten. Pray send my regards to Ludwig.\n\nYour loving husband,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080550,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":218,"prompt_tokens":932,"total_tokens":1150,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-w6qJoS94Qly4gL40OSdkLRfsFRImmcOO","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":932,"prompt_ms":921.897,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9891598712446352,"prompt_per_second":1010.958924912436,"predicted_n":218,"predicted_ms":5185.511,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.896364055299543,"predicted_per_second":41.84737049058424}}